# Implementation Plan - Timelapse Video Time Range & Playback Speed Adjustments

## 1. Overview & Problem Description
- **Issue 1 (Daytime Selection Time Range)**: For dates starting 23 September 2026 onwards, default and custom daytime timelapses select images from 3:00 AM to 3:00 PM instead of 6:00 AM to 6:00 PM local site time.
- **Issue 2 (Input Datetime Shift)**: When users select custom timelapse dates (e.g. `21-Sep-2026 00:00:00` to `22-Sep-2026 00:00:00`), DRF parsed naive inputs assuming server UTC, creating unexpected +3 hour offset shifts for Saudi Arabia (`Asia/Riyadh`).
- **Issue 3 (24-Hour Playback Speed)**: When "Include 24-Hour Images" is enabled, playback becomes noticeably slower between 9:00 PM and 11:59 PM due to frame/image density clustering during that window.

---

## 2. Impact Analysis: Does this Fix Impact Default Timelapse?
**YES, IT POSITIVELY FIXES DEFAULT TIMELAPSE AS WELL.**

Both **Default Timelapse** (automatically scheduled daily/monthly background jobs) and **Custom Timelapse** (on-demand user API requests) share the exact same underlying image retrieval clerk (`CameraImageDataDBFetcher`) and video generator engine (`S3CameraVideoV2`).

### Comparison Table

| Feature / Aspect | Default Timelapse (Scheduled) | Custom Timelapse (On-Demand) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Trigger Mechanism** | Background Celery Cron Schedule | User API Request (`POST /api/v1/project/9/camera/video-images/`) |
| **Shared Engine** | `CameraImageDataDBFetcher` + `S3CameraVideoV2` | `CameraImageDataDBFetcher` + `S3CameraVideoV2` |
| **Time Range Impact** | **Fixed**: Automatically selects 06:00 AM – 06:00 PM local site time across all dates. | **Fixed**: Automatically selects 06:00 AM – 06:00 PM local site time across all dates. |
| **24h Speed Impact** | N/A (Default timelapses are daytime-only). | **Fixed**: Eliminates 9 PM – 11:59 PM playback slowdown when `include_24_hours: true`. |

